[2026-10-25 13:00] Task: fix the PNG icon display (scaling and tinting).

What was found:
- The PNG assets are 284-432 px while the UI requested 12-26 px, and `IconButton._render` loaded them at native size and centred them in a small Canvas. Only the centre of each image was visible: the terminal glyph lives near the edges, so it disappeared; the trash body in the centre appeared as a red square.
- Tk's only downscale primitive is integer `subsample`; on these thin line icons it destroyed the strokes (terminal survived with 19/400 opaque pixels), so runtime subsampling was discarded.
- The asset branch also ignored the requested `color`, so hover/muted/active states and theme colours did not apply.

What was done:
- Kept the original large PNGs in `shellsuite/gui/assets/source/`.
