  The full logo (including the "ShellSuite" text) is letterboxed into 24x24 as requested.
- `shellsuite/gui/icons.py`: `load_asset(kind, size, color)` now loads the exact `<kind>-<size>-<role>.png`, maps theme colours to roles (`text`, `muted`, `accent`, `accent-hover`), caches `PhotoImage` objects, and returns `None` when a variant is absent so the Canvas vector icon is used instead. It never loads an unsized original.
- `shellsuite/gui/widgets.py`: `IconButton._render` passes the size and requested colour, so hover/active/muted changes now work for assets too.
- `pyproject.toml`: added `shellsuite.gui` package data for `assets/*.png`.

What was tested:
- `python -m unittest discover -s tests` -> 148 tests, all OK.
- Icon smoke: all 13 variants load at the requested dimensions with non-zero opaque pixels; required assets are used (24/24 IconButtons in a rendered Shells view); `chevron` and unknown colour roles still fall back to vector drawings.
